ompassion considering everything that  diet culture has taught us but  ultimately we don't have direct control  over our body or our weight there are  days or weeks like no joke when I feel  like I'm eating super healthy or  healthier than norm  and still for some reason out of the  blue my clothes don't fit well it's not  my fault it's just my body is doing  whatever it needs to do behaviors on the  other hand are things that I can  actually measure and actually change so  for me as an example a kind of easy or  compassionate behavior modification  might be to add like a serving of  veggies with my lunch or to make sure  that I have a really high protein  breakfast so that I don't leave the  house and then get ravenous mid-morning  and then eat like all the things later  on the other thing that I like to think  about is more about adding foods or  adding things to your diet rather than  thinking about taking them away so for  example if you're adding some lean  protein or healthy fats or fiber to your  dinner you're probably just gonna  naturally crowd out some of the late  night snacking or the treats without  feeling deprived as if you had said you  know I'm never eating cookies again  again I am NOT trying to tell you how to  lose weight I'm actually just kind of  giving you a bit of a sneak peek into  the gentle nutrition aspect of intuitive  eating and setting you up with some kind  of health minded tools to help you  achieve better nutrition status will you  lose weight no clue I don't know I don't  have control over that and ultimately  you don't really either but I'm hoping  that some of these little gentle  nutrition guidelines will just help to  improve your overall health but I just  want to say that if you've watched my  videos and you've thought to yourself or  you've said you know I just overeat  because something tastes good and I feel  better about everything when I'm on a  diet and pursuing intentional weight  loss this girl just does not get you I  do now I hear you and I am absolutely  here for you and I'm going to make sure  that there's a lot more content that  addresses some of your needs I hope you  will all continue to stick around and  learn with me it really means the world  so on that note if you liked this video  please be sure to give it the thumbs up  leave me a comment below with any  questions that you guys would have for  an upcoming video  subscribe to the channel and I'll see  you next time on Abby's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

